WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.580
It's a sort of Mount Everest Question that
you just want to solve because . . . The discovery

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.510
is a major breakthrough on a subject that
has bedeviled mathematicians since ancient

00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:26.610
times . . . This new result by Yitang Zhang,
which says that there are actually infinitely

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:31.920
many pairs of primes, which are separated
by no more than about 70 million.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:39.700
News started spreading through Twitter that
some mathematician had proved that prime gaps

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:40.870
were bounded.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.729
So when I saw that I was immediately interested,
and I started calling up some mathematicians

00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:47.040
and saying, "Is this real?

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:48.690
Who is this person?"

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.690
Never heard of him.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:56.721
Absolutely never heard of him, and when I
heard a rumor about that it was possible that

00:00:56.721 --> 00:01:00.910
this was done and roughly what techniques
were used, I said there's no way somebody

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:04.180
I've never heard of had done this.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:10.330
I mean really unusual to have someone like
sort of outside the math world or just on

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:14.420
the fringe of it, just come up with this kind
of result.

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:17.420
And he basically seems pretty normal.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.610
I really believe that mathematics should be
very pure.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.280
I love math.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.430
No one taught me but myself.

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:40.340
I like to read to learn and to think.

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:47.020
Although we say that mathematics should be
logical — of course it is logical — but

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.860
at the very beginning you are thinking.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.370
You are feeling.

00:01:50.370 --> 00:01:57.010
This seems very unclear, then you try to make
it clearer and clearer again.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.120
That could be intuition.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.600
Intuition is sometimes hard to describe
by words.

